From ab9a13f0eedda00bf852d22d37e23c9bf716e79f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:42:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a Claude Code call made before its input is written
 reached the client with no arguments

What changed

Claude Code 2.1.314 makes the calls of one message side by side, so a
second call can arrive through the MCP helper while its input is still
being streamed, carrying no arguments field at all. The run's fast
path (a call the transcript has not yet, tells the client itself)
emitted that shape as it came, and the client received a function_call
with empty arguments that could only fail; the message written seconds
later carried the input whole and was left out with the rest. A call
that arrived between the client's replies ended the same way, its
block dropped with its message.

Such a call is now held back and told by that message itself: a
message with a held call is no longer left out, its blocks the calls
already told are skipped, and every held call goes out with its whole
input (#4611).

Run

go test ./internal/gateway -run 'TestClaudeTUI' -count=1

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
